# Line endings are a correctness issue in this repo, not a style preference.
#
# packaging/mac/install.sh shipped once with CRLF endings and could not run on
# any Mac at all: /bin/bash treats the carriage return as part of the word, so
# `set -euo pipefail\r` becomes "set: : invalid option name" and the script
# dies having installed nothing. The first person to try it hit exactly that.
#
# Git on Windows will happily convert LF to CRLF in the working tree
# (core.autocrlf), which would reintroduce that bug for anyone who clones here
# and then builds a release. These rules pin the endings per file type so the
# checkout is correct regardless of anyone's git config.

# Normalize everything in the repository to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# POSIX shell and anything a Mac or Linux box executes: LF, always.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely want CRLF; cmd.exe is the fussy one.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries - a "line ending fix" inside these corrupts them.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.whl           binary
*.zip           binary
*.onnx          binary
*.db            binary
